      {
        "title": "Jul 30, 2026",
        "commits": [
          {
            "oid": "0f42eac25e44090837e92304ac08d8d430ceef0a",
            "url": "/react/react/commit/0f42eac25e44090837e92304ac08d8d430ceef0a",
            "authoredDate": "2026-07-30T21:17:49.000+01:00",
            "committedDate": "2026-07-30T21:17:49.000+01:00",
            "shortMessage": "[DevTools] Reset extension backend on pagehide (#37155)",
            "shortMessageMarkdown": null,
            "shortMessageMarkdownLink": "<a data-pjax=\"true\" title=\"[DevTools] Reset extension backend on pagehide (#37155)\n\nI have noticed inconsistency errors being thrown during browser\nnavigations that involve entries from BFCache. The main argument on why\nthis could be affecting React DevTools backend lifecycle is the fact\nthat Chrome kills the port manually, while freezing and preserving the\nJavaScript heap -\nhttps://developer.chrome.com/blog/bfcache-extension-messaging-changes.\n\nBasically, we could end up in a permutation, where port is dead, but\nBackend / Agent are alive. Such setup is not expected by React DevTools.\n\nOn `main`:\n\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9ca10286-b545-4384-bd6b-33d9a4ddde3d\n\n\nWith these changes:\n\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c4639c4a-6385-4248-a5c4-a39895d7fff6\n\n\nI couldn't come up with a good test for this yet, but I will try to add\nsomething. I am not convinced yet that emulating `pagehide` / `pageshow`\nwould be sufficient to reproduce browser environment during BFCache\nentries.\" class=\"color-fg-default\" href=\"/react/react/commit/0f42eac25e44090837e92304ac08d8d430ceef0a\">[DevTools] Reset extension backend on pagehide (</a><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5021573725\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/react/react/issues/37155\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/react/react/pull/37155/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/react/react/pull/37155\">#37155</a><a data-pjax=\"true\" title=\"[DevTools] Reset extension backend on pagehide (#37155)\n\nI have noticed inconsistency errors being thrown during browser\nnavigations that involve entries from BFCache. The main argument on why\nthis could be affecting React DevTools backend lifecycle is the fact\nthat Chrome kills the port manually, while freezing and preserving the\nJavaScript heap -\nhttps://developer.chrome.com/blog/bfcache-extension-messaging-changes.\n\nBasically, we could end up in a permutation, where port is dead, but\nBackend / Agent are alive. Such setup is not expected by React DevTools.\n\nOn `main`:\n\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9ca10286-b545-4384-bd6b-33d9a4ddde3d\n\n\nWith these changes:\n\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c4639c4a-6385-4248-a5c4-a39895d7fff6\n\n\nI couldn't come up with a good test for this yet, but I will try to add\nsomething. I am not convinced yet that emulating `pagehide` / `pageshow`\nwould be sufficient to reproduce browser environment during BFCache\nentries.\" class=\"color-fg-default\" href=\"/react/react/commit/0f42eac25e44090837e92304ac08d8d430ceef0a\">)</a>",
            "bodyMessageHtml": "I have noticed inconsistency errors being thrown during browser\nnavigations that involve entries from BFCache. The main argument on why\nthis could be affecting React DevTools backend lifecycle is the fact\nthat Chrome kills the port manually, while freezing and preserving the\nJavaScript heap -\n<a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/blog/bfcache-extension-messaging-changes\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.chrome.com/blog/bfcache-extension-messaging-changes</a>.\n\nBasically, we could end up in a permutation, where port is dead, but\nBackend / Agent are alive. Such setup is not expected by React DevTools.\n\nOn `main`:\n\n\n<a href=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9ca10286-b545-4384-bd6b-33d9a4ddde3d\">https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9ca10286-b545-4384-bd6b-33d9a4ddde3d</a>\n\n\nWith these changes:\n\n\n<a href=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c4639c4a-6385-4248-a5c4-a39895d7fff6\">https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c4639c4a-6385-4248-a5c4-a39895d7fff6</a>\n\n\nI couldn't come up with a good test for this yet, but I will try to add\nsomething. I am not convinced yet that emulating `pagehide` / `pageshow`\nwould be sufficient to reproduce browser environment during BFCache\nentries.",
            "authors": [
              {
                "login": "hoxyq",
                "displayName": "Ruslan Lesiutin",
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28902667?v=4",
                "path": "/hoxyq",
                "profileName": "Ruslan Lesiutin",
                "isGitHub": false
