          {
            "oid": "7acf00566e35c40817342654438a5757c6c41d0e",
            "url": "/react/react/commit/7acf00566e35c40817342654438a5757c6c41d0e",
            "authoredDate": "2026-07-30T21:17:48.000+01:00",
            "committedDate": "2026-07-30T21:17:48.000+01:00",
            "shortMessage": "[DevTools] Create extension panels before React detection (#37151)",
            "shortMessageMarkdown": null,
            "shortMessageMarkdownLink": "<a data-pjax=\"true\" title=\"[DevTools] Create extension panels before React detection (#37151)\n\nThe main reason why I am doing this is because there is no API in the\nbrowser to &quot;unmount&quot; the created panel.\n\nIf you have React DevTools installed, we should always create a panel,\nbut the contents of the panel should be dynamically populated based on\nthe target. If it is not a React app, we will continue showing the stub\nmessage.\n\nPreviously, we wouldn't mount a panel at all, and historically we've\nreceived a few reports of this as a bug.\" class=\"color-fg-default\" href=\"/react/react/commit/7acf00566e35c40817342654438a5757c6c41d0e\">[DevTools] Create extension panels before React detection (</a><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5020451264\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/react/react/issues/37151\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/react/react/pull/37151/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/react/react/pull/37151\">#37151</a><a data-pjax=\"true\" title=\"[DevTools] Create extension panels before React detection (#37151)\n\nThe main reason why I am doing this is because there is no API in the\nbrowser to &quot;unmount&quot; the created panel.\n\nIf you have React DevTools installed, we should always create a panel,\nbut the contents of the panel should be dynamically populated based on\nthe target. If it is not a React app, we will continue showing the stub\nmessage.\n\nPreviously, we wouldn't mount a panel at all, and historically we've\nreceived a few reports of this as a bug.\" class=\"color-fg-default\" href=\"/react/react/commit/7acf00566e35c40817342654438a5757c6c41d0e\">)</a>",
            "bodyMessageHtml": "The main reason why I am doing this is because there is no API in the\nbrowser to \"unmount\" the created panel.\n\nIf you have React DevTools installed, we should always create a panel,\nbut the contents of the panel should be dynamically populated based on\nthe target. If it is not a React app, we will continue showing the stub\nmessage.\n\nPreviously, we wouldn't mount a panel at all, and historically we've\nreceived a few reports of this as a bug.",
